# SEO package overview

This repo is `foodineers/seo` (`Foodineers\SEO`). One `SEOData` object becomes HTML head tags (title, meta, OG, Twitter, alternates, favicon, robots, canonical, sitemap, JSON-LD).

**Code under `src/` is the source of truth — not the README.** README still mentions removed APIs (`HasSEO`, `SchemaCollection`, `alternates`, `seo()->for($model)`). Prefer `SEOData`, `TagManager`, `SEOService`, and Pest suites.

## Mental model

1. Build `Foodineers\SEO\Support\SEOData` (named args; omit unknowns).
2. Pass to `SEOService::setData()` (usually `@seo`).
3. `TagManager::for()` clones + normalizes (config, URLs, title inference, `noindex`).
4. `TagCollection` builds tags; null tags are filtered out.
5. `render()` concatenates remaining `Renderable`s.

Never invent a second SEO data shape. Extend `SEOData` + a tag class + tests for new fields.

## Layout

```
src/SEOService.php | SEOServiceProvider.php | TagManager.php | TagCollection.php
src/Support/SEOData.php | ImageMeta.php | SchemaResolver.php | SchemaTagCollection.php
src/Tags/*  — one concern per tag; `initialize(?SEOData): ?Renderable`
```

## Do / don't

**Do:** treat `SEOData` as the public API; use `lang` for hreflang; Spatie `Schema::*` / `Graph` for JSON-LD; set `type: 'article'` before article OG fields; let `TagManager` absolutize relative image/favicon paths.

**Don't:** implement `HasSEO` / Eloquent `seo` / `getDynamicSEOData` unless re-added to `src/`; use README `SchemaCollection` / `alternates`; bypass `SEOData` with raw HTML; put business logic in tag `initialize` beyond field→markup; assume title suffix / homepage_title config keys exist.
